a couple of weeks ago I did a segment  where I told you that I had really been  sort of feeling down about the state of  affairs of American politics so much so  that I started kind of questioning is it  time for the David Pakman show to end  have we sort of done everything we could  do and that's it and it's time to hang  it up and ultimately I decided that no  way this is the worst possible time to  scale down and in fact we should really  be thinking about how to scale up  because we are at a time when  independent progressive need media is  arguably more needed than ever before  sort of sort of in the modern  independent media era and if it's been a  couple weeks now since that show and  I've been thinking about okay well if we  want to scale up what should be the next  thing what should be the scale up  because we've already done so many of  the things that we can do right growing  the show from once every other week to  daily expanding the staff to to  full-time producers upgrading equipment  improving graphics adding new  distribution platforms all that stuff so  to figure out what we should do next  I really just went back to what are the  most common complaints about the show  and I don't mean like hatred type  complaints obviously personal attacks  like I'm a Jew [ __ ] all of that stuff  those are some of the most common  complaints but what I mean is  constructive criticism right  constructive criticism and ideas from  our core audience and from our affiliate  television and radio stations and the  core complaints summed up basically are  not enough shows commercial breaks are  too long right I'm gonna deal with the  two complaints individually but I see  that as a good sign that the primary  complaint from our core audience and our  affiliate stations is we want more  content from you both in each show and  on a month-to-month and year-over-year  basis so let's first start with more  shows per year right now our limitations  are basically staffing limitations right  when we're on break there are no shows  because everyone takes vacation at the  same time we don't have sort of like two  sets of staff where we can wrote  vacations so the solution is we need to  add another person to the team and the  program started as just me then we had  me plus a part time producer then years  ago the position formal formerly held by  producer Louis went from part-time to  full-time then we added another  part-time producer which became a second  full-time producer at the beginning of  2018 so the next step is we add another  part-time position with the idea that if  things go well and we continue to grow  that position would become a third  full-time staff position on the show in  addition to me and that person would do  many things very important things but  one thing that they would do is learn  how to produce the show which would let  us start to rotate vacations Pat can go  on vacation and the new producer can  produce the show with me hosting Pat  comes back I can then go on vacation and  we can have a guest host host the show  with Pat producing and we've had a few  different guest hosts over the last year  we've got another one scheduled that you  will be meeting in the next couple of  weeks but the idea would be to have a  rotating cast of guest hosts and this  would allow us this is no joke this  would allow us to add about 25 shows per  year which is if you think about it on a  yearly basis that is a huge increase in  the number of new shows that we're going  to be able to produce and that's without  anybody losing vacation time which is a  really important thing to me as people  who watch the show listen to the show no  that's initiative number one secondly  let's talk about the commercial breaks  historically we used to have mostly like  long term advertisers sort of like  foundational underwriters that advertise  with us for an entire year at a time and  we still have some of those they're  different on the radio show on the  podcast different versions of the show  the show is a one hour show on broadcast  radio and TV so that's sort of like the  maximum time there's 60 minutes in an  hour corporate news hours are often 37  to 38 minutes we started with a 45  minute hour which was already a longer  hour  most corporate shows we then expanded  that hour to 49 minutes an hour some  time ago don't remember exactly how long  ago and because of the really great work  of producer Noah who's been working with  advertisers we are now in a position to  be able to cut a bunch of those ongoing  advertisers basically just say hey you  know what we are ending your sponsorship  of the David Pakman show which will  allow us to add time to the show because  most of these new advertisers are only  on our podcast and our YouTube channel  which is not restricted to an hour or  per show so what we're going to be able  to do with just a little bit of a push  is pull off some of those advertisers  and add that time directly to the show  which is going to give us about a 10  percent 10 12 percent longer hour every  single show how are we going to do this  am I going to do an IndieGoGo campaign  am i doing a membership drive is it  gonna be patreon the answer is no it's  actually gonna be much more simple  my goal is add 500 new paid supporters  to the show and in the past we've had  the problem where I do a membership  drive and patrons get upset or I talk  about YouTube's sponsorship and members  say I just signed up for membership and  now I don't count towards your new goal  so we are going to be in keeping with  the mo of the show  I am completely agnostic as to which  platform you use to count towards these  500 supporters the goal is 500 new  supporters and we're going to be  tracking this and there will be three  ways to help us three ways to count  towards that 500 number today is the  baseline today we start at zero option  number one become a member okay you go  to david pakman.com slash membership  monthly membership yearly membership use  the 40% off coupon code if you want  which is vote soon 18 which you can  enter on the second page of the signup  lots of great benefits including the  bonus show the commercial free audio and  video streams every new member at  whatever price counts towards our goal  of 500 new financial supporters second  method  counts just as much patreon how much do  you have to donate doesn't matter a  single dollar contribution counts as a  patreon donor at patreon.com slash david  pakman show and it counts towards the  goal of 500 new supporters also a lot of  really great perks on patreon and the  third option this is something new  perfectly welcome as well YouTube  sponsorship were part of a YouTube beta  for sponsorship which is $4.99 a month  it has its own set of benefits which  include a sponsors only icon next to  your name and comments and Chad sponsors  only posts you will see on the david  pakman show youtube channel as well as  on the video pages a sponsor button not  everybody will see it because it is in  beta sometimes you have to reload  there's some algorithm that determines  whether you see it or not but that will  also count to towards that 500 new  supporter number so membership patreon  YouTube sponsorship doesn't matter which  you do this will allow us to hire a new  producer create a new position to serve  as a backup producer 25 extra shows a  year shows will be 10% longer we also  will be able to with this new producer  to expand the show there's like three to  five new platforms that I would love to  be putting our content on but we're  simply maxed out right now with current  staffing so there is a lot we will be  able to do if you want more show help us  get to these 500 new supporters I will  update you tomorrow as to how it's going

